's part of  the reason why prices are slightly  higher like i say it's not everything  there's all sorts of factors going on at  the same time which are pushing up gas  prices around europe but that's one of  the issues in the uk and when you look  at what's happened to wind speeds in the  uk over the past 20 years that's your  historic range through the year look at  what's happened in 2021 they've really  been quite low and that's just going up  to july we're expecting quite low  numbers for august and september as well  so low wind some issues with high gas  prices it's all added up to what a lot  of people are calling the supply crisis
 

